# Files git must never touch the line endings of.
#
# This repository is worked on from Windows with core.autocrlf on, and git
# guesses whether a file is text by looking at its first few kilobytes. A PDF
# guesses wrong: docs/Pluggz-Deployment-Status.pdf came back out of a checkout
# 117 bytes larger than it went in, because every 0x0A inside it had been
# rewritten as 0x0D 0x0A. That shifts every byte offset in the file's own
# cross-reference table — the client-facing documents were being quietly
# damaged by cloning the repository.
#
# Images survive the same guess only because they happen to contain a null
# byte early on. They are listed anyway rather than relying on that.

*.pdf   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.avif  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4   binary
*.zip   binary
